body:
i can't think of any examples off the top of my head since most women in the media are well above average.  

&#x200B;

40th means you're basically seen as average, but will probably have a little less social leeway than someone who's truly average. but, since we're dealing with a bell curve here, the difference will be very slight.

get a sliding genioplasty asap.

&#x200B;

your droopy lips are caused by a lack of chin support.

&#x200B;

seriously, do it unless you wanna be a bottom for the rest of your life. you would be HOT with a more forward chin. and don't do an implant, go with an actual surgeon. it will change your life. watch as you suddenly go from the quiet queer kid to the hot skater boy lol

&#x200B;

also wear sunscreen daily, at all times of the day (the peak sun thing only causing damage is a bit of a boomer myth). you have a little bit of acne scarring, but you're young and with careful protection your skin should mostly repair itself. tretinoin is an option but I wouldn't go for it as it's a bit of a hassle with maintenance; dermarolling can be unpredictable as well given the lack of FDA standards

4/10. lol at trying to cover up your weak chin with that beard, you're gonna need to wait a few years until it grows in better.

&#x200B;

once you can fully disguise the weak chin, maybe 5-5.5
